<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">10 July in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">9 events that happened on 10 July, from 645 to 1962.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/soga-clan" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/soga-clan.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">645 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,381 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Prince Naka no Ōe assassinates Soga no Iruka</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Prince Naka no Ōe and Nakatomi no Kamatari killed the minister Soga no Iruka, beginning the Isshi incident, a plot to eliminate the main branch of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soga-clan">Soga clan</a>. The end of Soga power opened the way to the Taika reforms.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soga-clan">Soga clan</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1372 CE <span class="tih-ago">654 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Portugal and John of Gaunt sign the Treaty of Tagilde</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">King Ferdinand I of Portugal and representatives of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-of-gaunt">John of Gaunt, Duke of Lancaster</a> and claimant to the Crown of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-castile">Castile</a>, signed a treaty at the village of Tagilde. It is considered the first legal foundation of the Anglo-Portuguese Alliance.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-of-gaunt">John of Gaunt</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1460">1460 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">566 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Earl of Warwick captures Henry VI at Northampton</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Near the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/river-nene">River Nene</a>, Richard Neville, Earl of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/warwick">Warwick</a>, and Edward, Earl of March, defeated the Lancastrian army of King Henry VI and took the king prisoner. It was the first battle in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> in which artillery was used.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-lancaster">House of Lancaster</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1553">1553 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">473 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Lady Jane Grey is proclaimed Queen of England</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Days after Edward VI's death, the Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/northumberland">Northumberland</a> had his Protestant daughter-in-law proclaimed queen to bar the Catholic <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mary-i-of-england">Mary Tudor</a>. Jane's reign lasted nine days; she was executed the following year.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1584">1584 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">442 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">William the Silent is assassinated in Delft</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Balthasar Gérard shot William of Orange, leader of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> revolt against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, at his home in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delft">Delft</a>. He is often cited as the first head of state killed with a handgun.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1890">1890 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">136 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Wyoming becomes the 44th US state</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Wyoming joined the Union with women's suffrage intact; as a territory it had given women the vote in 1869. Congress accepted the state despite opposition to its equal-suffrage clause.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1925">1925 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">101 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Scopes 'Monkey Trial' opens in Tennessee</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Teacher John Scopes went on trial in Dayton for teaching human evolution. The clash between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/glarentza">Clarence</a> Darrow and William Jennings Bryan turned a local case into a national debate on science and faith.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1940">1940 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">86 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Battle of Britain begins</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luftwaffe">Luftwaffe</a> began attacking Channel convoys and coastal targets, the date <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> uses for the start of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-britain">Battle of Britain</a>. The RAF's survival over four months forced Hitler to postpone his invasion.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1962">1962 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">64 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Telstar is launched, the first satellite to relay live TV</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">NASA launched AT&amp;T's Telstar 1 from Cape Canaveral. Within hours it relayed the first television pictures across the Atlantic, opening the age of satellite communications.</p></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 10 July <span class="n">5</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/john-calvin"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/john-calvin.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">John Calvin</span><span class="tp">1509–1564</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/prince-maximilian-of-baden"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/prince-maximilian-of-baden.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Prince Maximilian of Baden</span><span class="tp">1867–1929</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/mahathir-mohamad"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/mahathir-mohamad.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Mahathir Mohamad</span><span class="tp">b. 1925</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/alice-munro"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/alice-munro.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Alice Munro</span><span class="tp">1931–2024</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/to-lam"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Tô Lâm</span><span class="tp">b. 1957</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 10 July <span class="n">9</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/leopold-i-margrave-of-austria"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/leopold-i-margrave-of-austria.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Leopold I, Margrave of Austria</span><span class="tp">d. 994</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/ladislaus-iv-of-hungary"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ladislaus-iv-of-hungary.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Ladislaus IV of Hungary</span><span class="tp">1262–1290</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/james-ii-of-cyprus"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/james-ii-of-cyprus.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">James II of Cyprus</span><span class="tp">c. 1438–1473</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/rene-of-anjou"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/rene-of-anjou.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">René of Anjou</span><span class="tp">1409–1480</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/catherine-cornaro"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/catherine-cornaro.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Catherine Cornaro</span><span class="tp">1454–1510</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/henry-ii-of-france"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/henry-ii-of-france.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Henry II of France</span><span class="tp">1519–1559</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/william-the-silent"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/william-the-silent.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">William the Silent</span><span class="tp">1533–1584</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/charles-ii-archduke-of-austria"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/charles-ii-archduke-of-austria.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Charles II, Archduke of Austria</span><span class="tp">1540–1590</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/fernando-pereira"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Fernando Pereira</span><span class="tp">1950–1985</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
